row
  col
    link "Accordion (Sections With Show/Hide Functionality)" accordion/
    text An accordion is a vertically stacked set of interactive headings that each contain a title, content snippet, or thumbnail representing a section of content.
  col
    link Alert alert/
    text An alert is an element that displays a brief, important message in a way that attracts the user's attention without interrupting the user's task.
  col
    link "Alert and Message Dialogs" alertdialog/
    text An alert dialog is a modal dialog that interrupts the user's workflow to communicate an important message and acquire a response.
  col
    link Breadcrumb breadcrumb/
    text A breadcrumb trail consists of a list of links to the parent pages of the current page in hierarchical order.
  col
    link Button button/
    text A button is a widget that enables users to trigger an action or event, such as submitting a form, opening a dialog, canceling an action, or performing a delete operation.
  col
    link "Carousel (Slide Show or Image Rotator)" carousel/
    text A carousel presents a set of items, referred to as slides, by sequentially displaying a subset of one or more slides.
  col
    link Checkbox checkbox/
    text WAI-ARIA supports two types of checkbox widgets: dual-state checkboxes toggle between two choices -- checked and not checked -- and tri-state checkboxes, which allow an additional third state known as partially checked.
  col
    link Combobox combobox/
    text A combobox is an input widget that has an associated popup.
  col
    link "Dialog (Modal)" dialog-modal/
    text A dialog is a window overlaid on either the primary window or another dialog window.
  col
    link "Disclosure (Show/Hide)" disclosure/
    text A disclosure is a widget that enables content to be either collapsed (hidden) or expanded (visible).
  col
    link Feed feed/
    text A feed is a section of a page that automatically loads new sections of content as the user scrolls.
  col
    link "Grid (Interactive Tabular Data and Layout Containers)" grid/
    text A grid widget is a container that enables users to navigate the information or interactive elements it contains using directional navigation keys, such as arrow keys, Home, and End.
  col
    link Landmarks landmarks/
    text Landmarks are a set of eight roles that identify the major sections of a page.
  col
    link Link link/
    text A link widget provides an interactive reference to a resource.
  col
    link Listbox listbox/
    text A listbox widget presents a list of options and allows a user to select one or more of them.
  col
    link "Menu and Menubar" menubar/
    text A menu is a widget that offers a list of choices to the user, such as a set of actions or functions.
  col
    link "Menu Button" menu-button/
    text A menu button is a button that opens a menu as described in the Menu and Menubar Pattern.
  col
    link Meter meter/
    text A meter is a graphical display of a numeric value that varies within a defined range.
  col
    link "Radio Group" radio/
    text A radio group is a set of checkable buttons, known as radio buttons, where no more than one of the buttons can be checked at a time.
  col
    link Slider slider/
    text A slider is an input where the user selects a value from within a given range.
  col
    link "Slider (Multi-Thumb)" slider-multithumb/
    text A multi-thumb slider implements the Slider Pattern but includes two or more thumbs, often on a single rail.
  col
    link Spinbutton spinbutton/
    text A spinbutton is an input widget that restricts its value to a set or range of discrete values.
  col
    link Switch switch/
    text A switch is an input widget that allows users to choose one of two values: on or off.
  col
    link Table table/
    text Like an HTML table element, a WAI-ARIA table is a static tabular structure containing one or more rows that each contain one or more cells; it is not an interactive widget.
  col
    link Tabs tabs/
    text Tabs are a set of layered sections of content, known as tab panels, that display one panel of content at a time.
  col
    link Toolbar toolbar/
    text A toolbar is a container for grouping a set of controls, such as buttons, menubuttons, or checkboxes.
  col
    link Tooltip tooltip/
    text A tooltip is a popup that displays information related to an element when the element receives keyboard focus or the mouse hovers over it.
  col
    link "Tree View" treeview/
    text A tree view widget presents a hierarchical list.
  col
    link Treegrid treegrid/
    text A treegrid widget presents a hierarchical data grid consisting of tabular information that is editable or interactive.
  col
    link "Window Splitter" windowsplitter/
    text A window splitter is a moveable separator between two sections, or panes, of a window that enables users to change the relative size of the panes.
